# Without this file, Git relies on its own heuristics to decide whether a
# file is text or binary. That usually works, but "usually" has already
# caused real corruption once - a PNG that was byte-correct in every
# packaged zip arrived broken after a git push. Declaring binary types
# explicitly removes the ambiguity entirely, rather than trusting detection
# to get it right every time.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary

# Everything else in this repo is text and benefits from normal diffing -
# left to Git's default handling, which is what we actually want for these.
